  "term": "sympathetic nervous system",
  "definition": "The sympathetic nervous system is the thoracolumbar part of the autonomic nervous system that helps prepare the body to respond to stress, commonly described as fight-or-flight reactions. It sends signals from the spinal cord through sympathetic ganglia to body organs and often works in an opposing balance with the parasympathetic system.",
